                    "message": "Under what conditions does entity-manager restart?  This shouldn't be a production behavior."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If entity-manager goes away, gpiopresence should keep its config, not drop all of it.  This is a bug in gpiopresence."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Since the SIT forked i2cget millions of times in a short period for stress testing, causing an OOM and killing entity-manager, it was noticed that the cable objects in gpiopresence disappear when entity-manager is restarted."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019m not sure if this should be considered a bug in gpiopresence. Maintaining the association between entity-manager objects and gpiopresence objects also seems reasonable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
